---
/**
 * Plain Markdown tables inside an MDX body.
 *
 * Authored comparisons use <ComparisonTable>, which brings its own framed,
 * sticky-column shell. This is for the ordinary pipe tables in the prose: it
 * keeps the table's own horizontal scroll inside a focusable container, so a
 * wide table never widens the page on a phone and a keyboard user can still
 * scroll it.
 *
 * The <table> stays inside `.prose` so it keeps the shared table typography
 * from global.css; only its margin is dropped, because the frame around it owns
 * the spacing now.
 */
---

<div class="my-7 overflow-hidden rounded-card border border-ink-200 bg-surface shadow-card">
  <p class="border-b border-ink-200 bg-ink-50 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-ink-500 sm:hidden">
    Scroll sideways to see every column.
  </p>
  <div tabindex="0" class="overflow-x-auto overscroll-x-contain">
    <table class="my-0! w-full min-w-[38rem] border-collapse text-left">
      <slot />
    </table>
  </div>
</div>
